From cd5505534bc9a91345259afb68a2e3d4aac17153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:47:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban events: never resume at since=0; coalesce
 frame-driven board re-reads

Problem: on 2026-11-13 05:09-05:40 PST the MacBook Desktop logged 1.5k+
"Timed out connecting to Hermes backend" on GET /api/plugins/kanban/board per
30 min (hub 30 s, mini 6 s), plus /boards, hub-sync/status and session-labels
behind them. Card t_01a1d51dd4d1f0d9.

Why 1: the renderer re-read the board ~3-4x/s. The query
["kanban","board","hermes-hub","default",false] had dataUpdateCount 4350 after
55 min against a 60 s refetchInterval. A queryCache subscription showed every
fetch stack running p.onmessage -> onEventsFrame -> invalidateQueries.
Why 2: one /events socket was replaying the hub's whole task_events history.
CDP Network frames showed 200 events per frame (ids 56,799 -> 333,155 in about
90 s; the hub max is 1,193,569). Each frame invalidated board+boards+blocked,
and fetchBoard fans out to 3 gateways (+ /boards + hub-sync/tasks).
Why 3: the socket was opened with since=0. When the routed gateway's own
/board read fails, mergeBoards writes latest_event_id: 0. snapshotCursor() and
the post-fetch tail took any number as a cursor, and the server replays from 0
for an explicit since=0 (plugin_api._since_param).
Why 4: the hub /board read was already timing out because the link was
saturated (1.1 GB sent on the hub ssh master in 55 min), so 0 kept getting
cached. Superseded reads were never aborted, because fetchBoard ignores the
query signal and invalidateQueries' default cancelRefetch only orphans the
promise. Every frame therefore added more HTTP requests to the 50-socket pool,
past the request deadline. This is a feedback loop.
Root (happened): the snapshot cursor contract had no "unknown" value. 0 meant
both "board has no events" and "routed gateway did not answer", and the
socket treated it as a resume point. Event-frame invalidation was also
unbounded per frame.
Root (not caught): api.events-cursor tests covered only positive snapshot
cursors and one frame at a time. No test fed a merged board whose primary
failed, or a burst of frames.
Recurrence: an earlier fix made a missing since start at the tail
(_since_param docstring: "replaying every task_events row ... turned each open
into a refetch storm"). It covered the absent cursor but not a cursor of 0
fabricated by mergeBoards.

Countermeasures:
- symptom/root: knownCursor() accepts only positive cursors, so an unknown
  snapshot opens at the server tail (snapshotCursor + post-fetch tail).
  mergeBoards documents 0 = unknown.
- root: event frames refresh board/boards/blocked at most once per 2 s per
  connection (leading + one trailing), with cancelRefetch: false so an
  in-flight read is reused, not orphaned. Per-task detail invalidation stays
  immediate.
- detection: 3 new tests in api.events-cursor.test.ts. All 3 fail on base and
  pass with the fix. The whole plugins/kanban vitest suite passes (149).
- deferred: pluginSocket reconnects reuse the dial-time since, which replays
  everything since the first dial after a tunnel drop. The coalescing bounds
  its cost. Noted on the card.
